    "narrative": "For tonight's slate, **Drake Baldwin** stands as our highest-rated asset at a 67.39. His projection is bolstered by the matchup against Griffin Canning, whose 4.59 xERA offers a high-ceiling environment for a leadoff hitter. We are banking on **Drake Baldwin** to maximize plate appearances in what should be a favorable offensive setting. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (63.09) also projects as a strong play; despite facing an arm like Ian Seymour, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** leverages his dynamic platoon edge and the stability of the #3 spot to remain an essential building block for our 5x5 production. **Dominic Smith** (57.50) edges closer to our recommended start threshold thanks to a favorable platoon split against Canning, providing solid if unspectacular efficiency in the #6 hole.\n\nOur most difficult decision centered on **Jackson Merrill**, who fell just short of the starting lineup with a score of 39.87. While **Jackson Merrill** is a high-upside component of the Austin Waves, the optimizer penalized him heavily for a daunting matchup against Chris Sale. The 19% reduction in expected performance due to the elite skill profile of the opposing starter, compounded by an unfavorable platoon split, pushed **Jackson Merrill** below the threshold necessary to risk a precious game cap. Note that we remain thin at the top today as **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** are inactive due to scheduled team off-days, forcing us to rely on secondary options like **Brayan Rocchio** (44.53) to fill the gaps. All starters currently carry \"Lineup Pending\" status, so we must monitor the official cards to ensure our projected order\u2014and the associated efficiency bonuses for **Drake Baldwin** and **Brayan Rocchio**\u2014hold true before first pitch.",
